{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CesvoUMLj5eYZyMLUGdqZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DG4UkqRxCnvDj69VZpB7he","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"mkdir -p intent/0001-nightly-export-drops-null-region-rows && cat > intent/0001-nightly-export-drops-null-region-rows/intent.md <<'EOF'\n# Intent: The nightly export cannot be trusted to contain every row, and says nothing when it does not\nAuthor: ops, via JIRA-4412 (captured by bifrost17; no originator in the session). Status: draft.\n\n## Problem\nReported in JIRA-4412 by ops.\n\n- Input: the nightly export job, on its normal schedule, over the usual source table.\n- Expected: every source row appears in the exported CSV, or the run fails visibly.\n- Actual: rows whose `region` is null are absent from the CSV and the run reports success. No error, no warning, no non-zero exit that ops noticed.\n- Volume: about 1,200 rows per night.\n- First affected night: 2026-08-30. Behaviour has continued on every night since.\n- Evidence: the row count of `export_2026-09-01.csv` is short of the count of the same rows in the database.\n- The exact command that reproduces this, and the commit deployed on 2026-08-30, were not recorded in the ticket — see Open questions.\n\nNo cause is asserted here. Ops observed that the absent rows are the ones with a null `region`; whether the null is the reason has not been established.\n\n## Proposed outcome\nOps can take any night's export and confirm it holds one row for every source row for that night — and on any night where that is not true, the job fails in a way ops sees that same night rather than reporting success.\n\n## Affected users and systems\n- Ops, who run and watch the nightly job and who filed the ticket.\n- Whoever consumes `export_<date>.csv` downstream — not identified in the ticket, and they have been receiving short files since 2026-08-30 without being told.\n- The nightly export job itself and the database it reads. Neither is in this repository (`trig-a` holds only `README.md` and `.claude/`) — see Open questions.\n- Any row with a null `region`, and therefore whatever part of the business those roughly 1,200 rows a night represent.\n\n## Constraints\n- The two end states ops named are the only acceptable ones: the export is complete, or the run fails loudly. A short export that reports success is not acceptable, whatever the row count.\n- Whether a null `region` is itself valid data is not settled by this intent, and the answer must not be assumed while fixing the export.\n- This intent picks no cause and no fix. Detection, backfill and the null handling itself are design decisions, not intent decisions.\n- The exports already produced from 2026-08-30 onward exist downstream; whether they are corrected, reissued or left alone is ops' call, not one to make silently.\n\n## Open questions\n- Which repository or service owns the nightly export job? Nothing in `trig-a` matches. — ops, or whoever runs the schedule\n- What exact command or scheduled entry produces `export_<date>.csv`, and what commit was deployed on 2026-08-30? — ops\n- Was there a deploy, schema change or data change on or around 2026-08-30? — ops, from the deploy log\n- Are the missing rows exactly the null-`region` rows — does 1,200 match the count of null-`region` rows in the database for that night, with nothing else missing? — ops, from the database\n- Is 2026-08-30 the first night this happened, or the first night anyone looked? — ops\n- Who consumes `export_<date>.csv`, and what have they done with the short files since 2026-08-30? — ops\n- Do the nights already exported since 2026-08-30 need re-exporting, or is forward correctness enough? — ops\n- What does \"fails loudly\" mean concretely here: non-zero exit, a page, an email, a dashboard? Which one does ops actually see at night? — ops\nEOF\necho \"--- written ---\"; grep -n '‹\\|›' intent/0001-nightly-export-drops-null-region-rows